Fix the ownership authorization module raising an authorization error for every non-admin save/modify, including creating new objects, instead of correctly checking ownership against the object itself. Removing, copying, and modifying templates, menus, network interfaces, and the group item types also no longer crash with the same error, and copying an object now correctly requires ownership instead of always being denied for non-admins. A new object whose owners were never explicitly set is now auto-assigned to the creating user's own group (or, if they belong to several groups, the save is refused with an explanation instead of guessing), so non-admin users can create new objects without being immediately locked out of them. Power-cycling a system now also requires ownership. Also close a name-collision gap where a new object could be used to bypass the real owner of an already-existing, differently-owned object of the same name.
